FP6 app-ready: a helper connection without a surface does not block suspension.

Morph (Qt 6 + QtWebEngine) opens a second Wayland connection that never
creates a surface. Its qtmir Session stays "Starting", and since the combined
state of several sessions is the most active one, the application never
reaches "Suspended": it sits in SuspendingWaitSession and lomiri-app-launch
is never asked to pause it. Ignore surfaceless Starting sessions as long as
another session of the app has had a surface.
--- a/src/modules/QtMir/Application/application.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/QtMir/Application/application.cpp
@@ -765,8 +765,22 @@
         return m_sessions[0]->state();
     }
 
+    bool anyHadSurface = false;
+    for (auto session : m_sessions) {
+        if (session->hadSurface()) {
+            anyHadSurface = true;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
     SessionInterface::State combinedState = SessionInterface::Stopped;
     for (auto session : m_sessions) {
+        // FP6 app-ready: a helper connection that never shows a surface (Morph's
+        // QtWebEngine) must not keep the app "Starting" and block suspension.
+        if (anyHadSurface && !session->hadSurface()
+                && session->state() == SessionInterface::Starting) {
+            continue;
+        }
         if (session->state() > combinedState) {
             combinedState = session->state();
         }
